# Part I: The Mathematical Program

Obsmetrologia is a foundations program. Its wager is that relation is not a structure
placed on top of already-given objects, but the generative act from which the
objects, values, orders, logics, spaces, and invariants of mathematics are
recovered.

This makes the project more basic than a program that begins with sets, spaces,
categories, topoi, or schemes. Those are not rejected. They are re-situated. A
category is not the ambient language in which Obsmetrologia is first spoken; category
appears when predicating has generated oriented cells and their lawful morphisms.
Order is not assumed as the background of every construction; order appears when
settling has generated closure and comparison. Logic is not a primitive calculus;
logics appear as projections of the bilattice-valued hyperdoctrine produced by
positing and quantifying.

This is the sense in which the program can be read as prior to familiar categorical
foundations. It does not try to outdo category theory by adding more categorical
machinery at the top. It asks what must be generated for category theory itself to
become available.

The reader should therefore expect an unusual order of explanation. Obsmetrologia does
not start with a universe of objects and arrows. It starts with marks, then asks
which acts must occur before "object", "arrow", "truth", "order", "space", and
"invariant" become lawful words.

## Why the manual has to be large

A foundations program cannot be documented like a package. A package manual can
list definitions and examples because its foundations are shared with the reader.
Obsmetrologia cannot assume that shared floor. Its documentation must teach the floor,
the descent, the recurring four-corner shape, the status of received mathematics,
and the difference between a generated object and a familiar name.

The manual therefore needs room for several kinds of exposition:

* *Orientation* — what problem the program is solving, and what it refuses to take
  as primitive.
* *Descent* — the stepwise generation from mark through settling and beyond.
* *Recurrence* — why the same four-corner coherence cell reappears as articulation
  phase, bilattice charge, nuclear quartet, modal shape, and regime signature.
* *Recovery* — how received mathematics is recovered in-chain: category, order,
  equality, modal logic, linear logic, sheaves, cohomology, dynamics, and geometry.
* *Frontier* — how to state open claims without making them look proved.
* *Examples* — small worked readings that let a person learn the system without
  first reading every Lean module.

The goal is not to simplify the mathematics until it looks ordinary. The goal is to
give the reader enough footholds that the non-ordinary structure can be followed
honestly.

## What "foundational" means here

In ordinary mathematical writing, foundations often means a base language in which
other mathematics is encoded: set theory, type theory, category theory, topos
theory. Obsmetrologia uses Lean as its formal checking language, but Lean is not the
mathematical foundation being proposed. Lean is the proof instrument.

The proposed foundation is the generated chain itself:

* marks supply atomicity without relation;
* utterances supply the two-sided admission boundary;
* articulating supplies the first cell structure;
* predicating supplies oriented relational positions;
* positing supplies independent evidence-for and evidence-against;
* settling supplies closure, order, fixed points, and regime.

Everything else is downstream of that chain. This is a strong claim, and the manual
should treat it as such. It should not merely assert that received mathematics is a
projection. It should show, case by case, how the projection is recovered and what is lost
when it is mistaken for the foundation.

For example, a Boolean truth value is a projection of a bilattice charge after
discarding the independence of evidence-for and evidence-against. A classical
equality predicate is a derived diagonal image in one adjoint system, not an
ambient primitive. A category is a recovered structure of predication, not the
first thing one must believe in before relation can be spoken.

This is why the prose must be patient. The project is not merely changing names. It
is changing which things are allowed to explain which other things.

## The shape of the book

This manual is organized as a book, not as a heap of notes. Its shape is:

* *Part I: Orientation.* What Obsmetrologia is, what it takes as primitive, why the
  generator/generated discipline matters, and how to read a path as a proof.
* *Part II: The Descent.* Mark, utterance, articulating, predicating, positing,
  settling. Each chapter should define the generated object, the generating act,
  the new lawful vocabulary, and the familiar mathematics first recovered there.
* *Part III: The Recurring Four.* The four-corner cell across articulation,
  bilattice value, Klein-four symmetry, nuclear quartet, modal pair, and closure
  regime.
* *Part IV: Recovered Mathematics.* Category theory, order theory, residuation,
  equality, hyperdoctrines, sheaves, cohomology, linear logic, modal logic,
  dynamics, and geometry as generated projections rather than imported foundations.
* *Part V: Frontier and Method.* How new mathematics enters the program, how
  exploratory claims become blueprint nodes, how proved results become manual
  prose, and how to state scope without shrinking the theorem into something
  misleading.

The back matter then gives the library atlas and documentation instruments. Those
surfaces are essential for lookup and maintenance, but the main body is the
mathematical ascent from primitive admission to recovered mathematics.
